cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PHM-XAI in your research, please cite it using the metadata below."
title: "PHM-XAI: Engine-Aware Trustworthy Prognostics"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end prognostics pipeline for remaining useful life (RUL) and health
  index (HI) estimation on the NASA C-MAPSS turbofan dataset. Point predictions
  are extended with engine-disjoint calibrated conformal uncertainty intervals
  (including EARA-Conformal), post-hoc explanations (Integrated Gradients, SHAP,
  temporal relevance, ERI), and constraint-aware maintenance recommendations.
type: software
version: "0.1.0"
date-released: "2026-01-01"
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/me-intenzo/phm_project"
keywords:
  - prognostics
  - remaining useful life
  - RUL
  - predictive maintenance
  - explainable AI
  - conformal prediction
  - uncertainty quantification
  - C-MAPSS
  - turbofan
